---
import { COMPANY, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../config';
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

// These Terms replace Apple's standard licence agreement (decided 2026-11-25, PLAN.md), so they
// carry the minimum terms Apple requires of a custom licence agreement (section "Apple").
---

<Legal
  locale="en"
  path="/terms"
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms for using Riffu and its optional Pro subscription."
>
  <p>
    These Terms are an agreement between you and {COMPANY.name} ("we") for the use of the Riffu app
    and this website. By downloading or using Riffu, you accept them. If you do not accept them, do
    not use Riffu.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who can use Riffu</h2>
  <p>
    You must be 13 or older. If you are under 18, or under the age of majority where you live, you
    may use Riffu only with the permission of a parent or guardian, who accepts these Terms for you.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The service</h2>
  <p>
    Riffu teaches the saxophone and the clarinet with lessons, a tuner and practice tools. It is
    free to use. Pro is an optional subscription that adds more, as described in the app. We may
    add, change or remove features over time.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can use Riffu without an account. If you create one, keep access to your email address or
    Apple ID safe, because that is how you sign in. You can delete your account at any time; see
    <a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Pro subscriptions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pro is sold through the App Store and billed by Apple to your Apple ID.</li>
    <li>
      A subscription renews automatically at the end of each period unless you cancel it at least 24
      hours before the period ends. The renewal is charged within the 24 hours before the period
      ends.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where a free trial is offered, it turns into a paid subscription when it ends unless you
      cancel at least 24 hours before.
    </li>
    <li>
      To cancel, open your iPhone's Settings, tap your name, then Subscriptions. Deleting the app or
      your Riffu account does not cancel a subscription.
    </li>
    <li>
      Prices are shown in the App Store before you buy. Refunds are handled by Apple under its own
      policies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Use Riffu for your own learning. Do not copy, resell or redistribute it or its content, try to
    break or get around its security or its Pro features, reverse engineer it except where the law
    allows, or use it in a way that breaks the law or harms others.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Our content</h2>
  <p>
    Riffu, its lessons, music, drawings, the name Riffu and the character Melo belong to{' '}
    {COMPANY.name}
    or its licensors. We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the app
    on Apple devices that you own or control, as permitted by the Usage Rules in the Apple Media
    Services Terms and Conditions, except that it may also be accessed and used by other accounts
    associated with you through Family Sharing or volume purchasing.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    Riffu helps you practise; it does not guarantee any result, and it is not a substitute for a
    teacher where you need one. Play at a volume and for times that are safe for you. To the extent
    the law allows, Riffu is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, {COMPANY.name} is not liable for indirect, incidental or
    consequential damages, and its total liability to you is limited to the greater of the amount
    you paid for Riffu in the twelve months before the claim and 50 US dollars. Some places do not
    allow these limits, so they may not apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Ending</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Riffu and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or end access for
    anyone who breaks these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Apple</h2>
  <p>If you got Riffu from the App Store, these terms also apply:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      These Terms are between you and {COMPANY.name} only, not Apple. {COMPANY.name}, not Apple, is
      responsible for Riffu and its content.
    </li>
    <li>
      Apple has no obligation to provide any maintenance or support for Riffu. Write to us for
      support.
    </li>
    <li>
      If Riffu fails to conform to any warranty that applies, you may notify Apple, and Apple will
      refund the purchase price, if any. To the extent the law allows, Apple has no other warranty
      obligation for Riffu, and any other claims, losses or costs from a failure to conform to a
      warranty are our responsibility.
    </li>
    <li>
      {COMPANY.name}, not Apple, is responsible for any claims about Riffu, including product
      liability claims, claims that Riffu fails to meet a legal or regulatory requirement, and
      claims under consumer protection, privacy or similar laws.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a third party claims that Riffu or your use of it infringes their intellectual property,
      {COMPANY.name}, not Apple, is responsible for the investigation, defence, settlement and
      discharge of that claim.
    </li>
    <li>
      You confirm that you are not in a country subject to a United States Government embargo or
      designated as a "terrorist supporting" country, and that you are not on any United States
      Government list of prohibited or restricted parties.
    </li>
    <li>You must follow any third-party terms that apply when you use Riffu.</li>
    <li>
      Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms. Once you accept them,
      Apple has the right to enforce them against you as a third-party beneficiary.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of New Mexico, United States, without regard
    to its conflict of laws rules. Disputes go to the state or federal courts located in Bernalillo
    County, New Mexico, unless the law of the country where you live lets you bring them where you
    live. This does not take away any protection that the consumer law of the country where you live
    gives you.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms. If a change matters, we will say so in the app or on this page before
    it takes effect, and change the date at the top. If you keep using Riffu after that, you accept
    the new Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions, complaints and claims go to:</p>
  <address>
    {COMPANY.name}
    <br />
    {COMPANY.address}
    <br />
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
  </address>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle your data.
  </p>
</Legal>
